These are two independent if statements.

An else-if ladder would execute only one branch.


============================================================
84. if vs else-if
============================================================

Independent if statements:

    if (x > 0)
        printf("A");

    if (x > 5)
        printf("B");


If x = 10:

    AB


else-if:

    if (x > 0)
        printf("A");
    else if (x > 5)
        printf("B");


If x = 10:

    A


Only the first matching branch executes.


============================================================
85. NESTED if VS LOGICAL AND
============================================================

Nested:

    if (a)
    {
        if (b)
        {
            printf("Yes");
        }
    }


Equivalent in many simple cases:

    if (a && b)
    {
        printf("Yes");
    }


The second form is often cleaner.


============================================================
86. COMPLEX REAL-WORLD CONDITION
============================================================

Example:

    int age;
    int hasID;
    int isMember;

    if (age >= 18 &&
        hasID &&
        (isMember || age >= 60))
    {
        printf("Allowed");
    }


Break it down:

    age >= 18
        AND
    hasID
        AND
    (
        isMember
        OR
        age >= 60
    )


Use parentheses for clarity.


