89. BEST PRACTICES
============================================================

1. Always use braces for multi-statement blocks.

2. Use meaningful conditions.

3. Avoid deeply nested if statements.

4. Prefer guard clauses when appropriate.

5. Use switch for discrete constant choices.

6. Always consider break in switch.

7. Use default for unexpected choices.

8. Don't compare strings using ==.

9. Don't write chained mathematical comparisons.

10. Watch signed/unsigned comparisons.

11. Avoid floating-point equality when inappropriate.

12. Use parentheses for complex boolean expressions.

13. Enable compiler warnings.

Recommended:

