98. CHAPTER 7 QUICK REVISION
============================================================

if:

    One-way decision.

if-else:

    Two-way decision.

else-if:

    Multiple mutually exclusive branches.

nested if:

    Decision inside another decision.

switch:

    Multiple discrete constant choices.

case:

    Individual switch option.

default:

    Executes when no case matches.

break:

    Exits switch or loop.

fall-through:

    Execution continues into the next case when break
    is absent.

&&:

    Logical AND + short-circuit.

||:

    Logical OR + short-circuit.

!:

    Logical NOT.

?:

    Conditional operator.


