99. MOST IMPORTANT RULES
============================================================

RULE 1:

    0 = false
    non-zero = true


RULE 2:

    =  means assignment
    == means comparison


RULE 3:

Use:

    x >= 10 && x <= 20

not:

    10 <= x <= 20


RULE 4:

Use:

    x == 1 || x == 2 || x == 3

not:

    x == 1 || 2 || 3


RULE 5:

    && and || short-circuit.


RULE 6:

Use braces to avoid dangling-else and maintenance bugs.


RULE 7:

switch uses constant case labels.


RULE 8:

Remember break to prevent unintended fall-through.


RULE 9:

Use strcmp() for C string content comparison.


RULE 10:

Use if-else for ranges and complex conditions.


